{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu","id":1552567,"title":"The Azlu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-21T16:54:29-07:00","id":1552567,"title":"The Azlu","content":"I finally got Predators for WW:tF, and I thought the Ananasi were scary, but these guys, take the cake; even if a mortal should learn of their existence, it should require a morality/integrity-roll.<br /> <br /> Back in the day, I thought of running an ancient WW:tA, game, based thousands of years ago during the LCM (Last Glacial Maximum), on the lost continent of Sundra, with the Ananasis' running some sort of human-civilization (primitive horticulturalists), but now, yikes. It's like, someone said, &quot;You can make were-spiders more terrifying&quot;, and someone else said, &quot;Hold my beer&quot;. <br /> <br /> Has anyone used the Azlu in their games? How'd it go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T04:07:41-07:00","id":1552696,"title":"","content":"I haven't used the Azlu as I've not played alot of Werewolf due to it not being a popular game in my group.<br /> <br /> But I'm suprised there's been a week without a single mention of their use with the Azlu being one of the primary antagonists for the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-16T08:18:38-07:00","id":1553216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1552696#post1552696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't used the Azlu as I've not played alot of Werewolf due to it not being a popular game in my group.<br /> <br /> But I'm suprised there's been a week without a single mention of their use with the Azlu being one of the primary antagonists for the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to be playing Werewolf to use the Azlu as antagonists; no one would expect them in a regular NWoD-game. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-16T12:59:28-07:00","id":1553222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553216#post1553216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't have to be playing Werewolf to use the Azlu as antagonists; no one would expect them in a regular NWoD-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true I would think the most common place to find the Azlu would be in a Forsaken game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-25T19:46:50-07:00","id":1553452,"title":"","content":"I've used them in werewolf games and hunter ones. The hunters really weren't made to handle them using Werewolf rules so the Vigil rules allow for toned down variants. I just used the three in the Predators book, the Spectral Sentinel, the Eye Eater, and the Orchid Mother (along with assorted lesser minions).<br /> <br /> And that was just in 1e. In 2e they're basically instant death for most non-werewolves that get touched by them. Which can be good if you want to justify them turning a NPC into a host. But it can be a little much to expect a cell to hunt down a spider that may be an inch in diameter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T04:31:05-07:00","id":1553456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553452#post1553452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've used them in werewolf games and hunter ones. The hunters really weren't made to handle them using Werewolf rules so the Vigil rules allow for toned down variants. I just used the three in the Predators book, the Spectral Sentinel, the Eye Eater, and the Orchid Mother (along with assorted lesser minions).<br /> <br /> And that was just in 1e. In 2e they're basically instant death for most non-werewolves that get touched by them. Which can be good if you want to justify them turning a NPC into a host. But it can be a little much to expect a cell to hunt down a spider that may be an inch in diameter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can they not sure fire? Scorched earth tactics? I mean, assuming the fund the thing in the first place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T10:31:34-07:00","id":1553462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553456#post1553456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can they not sure fire? Scorched earth tactics? I mean, assuming the fund the thing in the first place...</div> </div> </div> </div>About to say instant death sounds very extreme using 2nd edition forsaken rules unless its an ambush. But that would go for most monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T00:43:25-07:00","id":1553475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553456#post1553456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can they not sure fire? Scorched earth tactics? I mean, assuming the fund the thing in the first place...</div> </div> </div> </div>This was with the hunters. Finding it was a big part of the problem with them. There's vermin everywhere and most hunters don't have a passive ability to tell one spider from an azlu. And while we did use the Dogs of War book in one of our games in most of them they didn't have the capability of destroying entire buildings and all living things in them. Especially since some can basically disappear from the world by stepping sideways.<br /> <br /> And them doing that in the first place would rely on them knowing what an azlu or beshilu or ukusgualu even are. The encounter with the Azlu was their first session. The cell was trying to intercept a shipment of occult books that was moving through the city, and in turn found it intercepted by regular gunmen led by men hosting lesser azlu. Car chase led them back to the azlu den, big fight, then high-fiving as all the spider-monsters and spider-mobsters were dead and a bunch of regular spiders scurried out without raising an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> After re-organizing, the azlu had Eye Eater find the cell and look into them but finding out that they weren't specifically after the azlu made them less of a concern.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553462#post1553462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About to say instant death sounds very extreme using 2nd edition forsaken rules unless its an ambush. But that would go for most monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it. I personally love it. As far as I can tell in 1e humans weren't really expected to be much of a deal in 1e, and no one was planning for Hunter the Vigil when Forsaken was being made. So they're dangerous for Forsaken but absolutely lethal for regular humans (which, to be fair, is what helps them become dangerous to Forsaken). It's the host thing. They're a rat, or a spider, and they crawl into you. The rat eats into your belly and then eats your heart. You're dead, just a fleshy Gundam for the beshilu now. No roll.<br /> <br /> Some of the supernatural folks might have powers that would let them pull a squirming rat out of you before it gets to your heart, or reach in your skull and crush a spider before it eats too much of your brain, but in 1e that was not really a guarantee to come across, especially in the short time span you had until the human's a puppet.<br /> <br /> In 2e it's a lot easier. &quot;To Join with a human, the shard makes contact with its victim's flesh. As an Instant action, it then invades their body. This gradually kills the human, eating through one level of Health per turn, after which the Shard takes control of the carcass...&quot; Sure, it sucks for Hunters, but they're not a hunter antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T12:38:40-07:00","id":1553490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553475#post1553475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was with the hunters. Finding it was a big part of the problem with them. There's vermin everywhere and most hunters don't have a passive ability to tell one spider from an azlu. And while we did use the Dogs of War book in one of our games in most of them they didn't have the capability of destroying entire buildings and all living things in them. Especially since some can basically disappear from the world by stepping sideways.<br /> <br /> And them doing that in the first place would rely on them knowing what an azlu or beshilu or ukusgualu even are. The encounter with the Azlu was their first session. The cell was trying to intercept a shipment of occult books that was moving through the city, and in turn found it intercepted by regular gunmen led by men hosting lesser azlu. Car chase led them back to the azlu den, big fight, then high-fiving as all the spider-monsters and spider-mobsters were dead and a bunch of regular spiders scurried out without raising an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> After re-organizing, the azlu had Eye Eater find the cell and look into them but finding out that they weren't specifically after the azlu made them less of a concern.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I get it. I personally love it. As far as I can tell in 1e humans weren't really expected to be much of a deal in 1e, and no one was planning for Hunter the Vigil when Forsaken was being made. So they're dangerous for Forsaken but absolutely lethal for regular humans (which, to be fair, is what helps them become dangerous to Forsaken). It's the host thing. They're a rat, or a spider, and they crawl into you. The rat eats into your belly and then eats your heart. You're dead, just a fleshy Gundam for the beshilu now. No roll.<br /> <br /> Some of the supernatural folks might have powers that would let them pull a squirming rat out of you before it gets to your heart, or reach in your skull and crush a spider before it eats too much of your brain, but in 1e that was not really a guarantee to come across, especially in the short time span you had until the human's a puppet.<br /> <br /> In 2e it's a lot easier. &quot;To Join with a human, the shard makes contact with its victim's flesh. As an Instant action, it then invades their body. This gradually kills the human, eating through one level of Health per turn, after which the Shard takes control of the carcass...&quot; Sure, it sucks for Hunters, but they're not a hunter antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get whatcha mean. Personally I would just house rule that, IF your character is aware, he can fight it off with a roll that wont be high target (which the vermin could always just try again). Otherwise id do plot for the sake PC characters not just getting picked as the Host body. <br /> <br /> However, I tend to play my games with a focus of how fragile hunters are, so i understand why you prefer to give them a relatively fair fighting chance.<br /> <br /> Plus, Werewolf shouldn't be balanced for Hunter anyway. I think youre &quot;right&quot; as to where im &quot;wrong&quot; in using Forsaken rules for Vigil games (had beshilu in the sewers of Dallas lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T14:24:16-07:00","id":1553817,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve used Azlu in a couple different games, in the cofd version of my home town I have an Azlu matron who rubs her multiple elbows with the vampires of the city, offering to have her daughters spin webs around their Havens to protect them from Uratha incursion spirit-side(The Iron Masters and Hunters-in-Darkness have been starting to realize the kindred and the spider hosts are in bed with each other for.. some nefarious reason.)<br /> <br /> In my Hunter game I was going to have the cell encounter an Hybrid Azlu was gonna menace and chase them around an abandoned State Hospital, but that game fell through.<br /> <br /> I think they\u2019re fun monsters to throw at the players, especially if they\u2019re scared of spiders &gt;:3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-21T09:43:27-07:00","id":1553957,"title":"","content":"The spider literally has to crawl and chew it's way from the ear-cavity to the brain; how much time in the material-world so the azlu-spiderling have? Most spiders, don't have jaws, so, they have to literally stab through flesh to get there; you'd think by then, a host would notice and a doctor could removed it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553817#post1553817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. ..<br /> <br /> I think they\u2019re fun monsters to throw at the players, especially if they\u2019re scared of spiders &gt;:3</div> </div> </div> </div>No kidding: <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6U5anqIpdvU?si=SGd0V300UR2erYlA\" data-code=\"6U5anqIpdvU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6U5anqIpdvU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T06:42:05-07:00","id":1553976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553957#post1553957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spider literally has to crawl and chew it's way from the ear-cavity to the brain; how much time in the material-world so the azlu-spiderling have? Most spiders, don't have jaws, so, they have to literally stab through flesh to get there; you'd think by then, a host would notice and a doctor could removed it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No kidding: <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6U5anqIpdvU?si=SGd0V300UR2erYlA\" data-code=\"6U5anqIpdvU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6U5anqIpdvU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't this explained in &quot;Predators&quot;? As I recall it primarily comes down to the Azlu's magic preventing the host from having more than a headache as the Azlu works, until its too late. But my memory isn't entirely clear on the details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-30T21:42:42-07:00","id":1554072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552567-the-azlu?p=1553957#post1553957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spider literally has to crawl and chew it's way from the ear-cavity to the brain; how much time in the material-world so the azlu-spiderling have? Most spiders, don't have jaws, so, they have to literally stab through flesh to get there; you'd think by then, a host would notice and a doctor could removed it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In either edition, it's not an entirely physical-world act. In 1e if they have the form of a particularly large spider then they can just &quot;shrink down to a tiny size.&quot; Then the spider &quot;Races though the skull and towards the brain.&quot; This isn't described as needing them to physically dig their way there. Even when they do get there, &quot;the spider begins to eat the brain, mystically digesting the host's memories along with the soft brain tissue.&quot; So it's not as if they can eat a spider-stomach worth, then have to stop to digest, then another spider-stomach worth and on and on. Think less of a real life leech or tick and more of a body-snatcher, you feel like crap and pop some Advil and try to take a nap and wake up Spider-man.<br /> <br /> &quot;The process takes approximately two to six hours.&quot; That could be done in the time it takes to get to a hospital and have it be your turn in the waiting room.<br /> <br /> In 2e it's far faster. &quot;To Join with a human, the Shard makes contact with its victim\u2019s flesh. As an Instant action, it then invades their body...This gradually kills the human, eating through one level of Health per turn, after which the Shard takes control of the carcass and gains the Discorporate Dread Power.&quot; So they can be done in less than a minute with all but the hardiest of humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-01-2025, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}